meta {
  name: Search pull requests
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: https://api.github.com/search/issues?q&per_page=100
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  q: 
  per_page: 100
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  ## Search query
  
  Here is an example you can use as reference search query (parameter `q`) to search pull requests:
  
  ```none
  <KEYWORD> is:pr created:2025-07-01..2025-07-15 -repo:<ORGANIZATION>/<REPO>
  ```
  
  Where:
  
  * `<KEYWORD>` is a search keyword.
  * `is:pr` specifies that result must include only pull requests.
  * `created:…` limits the result including only the pull requests created in the given interval.
  * `-repo:…` excludes the pull requests of the specified repository.
  
  ## Additional documentation
  
  * API documentation: [Searching issues and pull requests](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/search/search?apiVersion=2022-11-28#search-issues-and-pull-requests)
  * Search queries: [Searching issues and pull requests](https://docs.github.com/en/search-github/searching-on-github/searching-issues-and-pull-requests)
}
